WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.390 --> 00:00:04.319
Making a movie is a collaborative effort,
but at the end of the day, the director is

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.080
the one who's calling the shots, and sometimes
they get things very wrong.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:12.550
In fact, some of the greatest filmmakers in
history cringe when they remember certain

00:00:12.550 --> 00:00:14.060
moments from their own movies.

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:17.520
Here's a look at some scenes that directors
regret shooting at all.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:19.480
Cameron rewrites history

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:24.780
Titanic is one of the most popular films in
movie history, but not everyone is a fan thanks

00:00:24.789 --> 00:00:29.970
to some artistic liberties taken by writer-director
James Cameron regarding the story of the ship's

00:00:29.970 --> 00:00:32.540
first officer, William McMaster Murdoch.

00:00:32.650 --> 00:00:36.900
A real historical figure who lost his life
in the tragic sinking of the Titanic, some

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.400
theorize that Murdoch may have committed suicide.

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.960
Though there's no proof at all, Cameron decided
to run with it, even adding a bit where Murdoch

00:00:44.020 --> 00:00:45.660
shoots another character first.

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:47.760
Cameron explained to National Geographic

00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:51.660
"I took the liberty of showing [Murdoch] shoot
somebody and then shoot himself [...] We don't

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:55.140
know he did that, but you know, the storyteller
in me says, 'Oh.'

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:56.780
I start connecting the dots.

00:00:57.080 --> 00:01:01.360
He was on duty, he's carrying all this burden
with him, made him an interesting character."

00:01:01.600 --> 00:01:05.680
Residents of Murdoch's hometown protested
the scene, and Murdoch's nephew worried the

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:07.760
film would ruin his ancestor's name.

00:01:07.860 --> 00:01:09.660
Cameron ended up apologizing, saying,

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:13.680
"I wasn't thinking about being a historian,
and I think I wasn't as sensitive about the

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:17.720
fact that his family, his survivors, might
feel offended by that, and they were."

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:19.940
Coogler's tragic odyssey

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.340
You'd think that when it comes to Black Panther,
Ryan Coogler wouldn't have any regrets.

00:01:24.340 --> 00:01:28.800
It's the most critically acclaimed film in
the MCU, it's the ninth highest-grossing film

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:33.580
of all time, and it was genuinely a landmark
moment in the history of superhero movies.

00:01:33.640 --> 00:01:38.480
Still, Coogler told The Toronto Sun he regrets
getting rid of the villainous Ulysses Klaue,

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:40.540
played with verve by Andy Serkis.

00:01:40.800 --> 00:01:41.600
"I like Klaue.

00:01:41.600 --> 00:01:43.160
I was bugged by having to do that.

00:01:43.160 --> 00:01:46.920
It's tough when you have to kill characters
off, and I really did love that character.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:47.920
I love Andy.

00:01:47.920 --> 00:01:48.860
He's a lovely person.

00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:52.570
But again, it's one of those things where
when you've got so many people in a movie,

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:53.560
some of them have to go."

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:55.620
Abrams needs a hug

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.740
After the shocking death of Han Solo in Star
Wars: The Force Awakens, fans were in desperate

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:01.480
need of a hug.

00:02:01.760 --> 00:02:04.840
And so, presumably, was Han's life partner,
Chewbacca.

00:02:04.940 --> 00:02:09.160
Yet when he arrived back at the Rebel Base,
General Leia just walked right by him to offer

00:02:09.160 --> 00:02:11.400
solace to Rey, a total stranger.

00:02:11.460 --> 00:02:15.940
It's a scene that bugged a lot of people,
including director J.J. Abrams, who said he

00:02:15.940 --> 00:02:17.940
regrets the optics of the situation.

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:22.810
He told Slashfilm it looks a lot worse than
it was, as Chewie was preoccupied with getting

00:02:22.810 --> 00:02:25.060
the injured Finn some medical attention anyway.

00:02:25.180 --> 00:02:28.819
"Had Chewbacca not been where he was, you
probably wouldn't have thought of it.

00:02:28.819 --> 00:02:32.700
But because he was right there, passed by
Leia, it felt almost like a slight, which

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:34.300
was definitely not the intention."

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.440
Gluck insults Xenu

00:02:37.050 --> 00:02:41.240
Tom Cruise may be the face of Scientology,
but Hollywood is filled with plenty of other

00:02:41.240 --> 00:02:43.900
adherents, including actress Jenna Elfman.

00:02:44.060 --> 00:02:49.300
Unfortunately, while attending the first screening
of her 2011 film Friends with Benefits, Elfman

00:02:49.300 --> 00:02:54.000
was blindsided by a Scientology joke which
hadn't appeared in the script, and nobody

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:55.150
had warned her about it.

00:02:55.150 --> 00:02:58.760
“And if any of these cameras are hooked
up to the actual Scientology center, that

00:02:58.760 --> 00:02:59.910
was an inappropriate joke and I apologize.

00:02:59.910 --> 00:03:02.540
I believe in the freedom of science fiction.”

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:07.640
Director Will Gluck told IndieWire he regretted
how the joke played out.

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.920
"The way I work, I change the script a lot.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:13.250
While we're shooting, I'll yell out, 'Try
this, try that!'

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:15.269
We shot [the joke] once and then we left it
in.

00:03:15.269 --> 00:03:18.690
But I feel really bad because I didn't tell
Jenna about it, and then I forgot."

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:19.440
Whoops!

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:21.720
Gluck triggers a reaction

00:03:22.180 --> 00:03:26.020
After the Scientology fiasco, you'd think
director Will Gluck would have learned his

00:03:26.020 --> 00:03:26.520
lesson.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:31.940
But in the 2018 film Peter Rabbit, Gluck incited
an uproar thanks to a scene where the supposedly

00:03:31.950 --> 00:03:37.349
cute rabbits intentionally trigger a nearly
fatal allergic reaction in Domhnall Gleeson's

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:39.560
character by attacking him with blackberries.

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:44.659
The scene led to major backlash online, and
Asthma and Allergy Foundation of America even

00:03:44.660 --> 00:03:49.180
weighed in, condemning the sequence for making
light of such a serious issue in a children's

00:03:49.180 --> 00:03:49.680
film.

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.540
As a result, Gluck and Sony Picture formally
apologized, saying that they were... berry,

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:55.359
berry sorry.

